{
  "_doc": "T-175: the Crucible's room on every map, built at load by gravelight/world/crucible_room.gd (MapRoot attaches it). Every position is in the Crucible's own frame: origin = the floor under its centre, local -Z = its front (where you stand to feed it), +Y up, metres. A map is keyed by its id up to the first underscore. pieces: box, cyl, pipe (points, r, glass, valve), tank (r, h, face), bench (w, d, h; yaw turns it about `at`; its work side is local -Z), ledger (stacks of the Ledger's books on a surface at h), cable (a, b, sag), grate (lo, hi: the flat dais), ring (Marke dashes on the floor round `at`), frame (a portal round the machine), hood, rack (wall tools), drum, crate, lamp (a fixture; its light is a `lights` entry), notice (paper + Label3D text, local -Z out of the wall), chain. Rules (tests/unit/test_crucible_rooms.gd): a piece's primitives stay off the baked navmesh unless flat on the floor (<= 0.06 m) or over head height (>= 2.05 m), nothing but a flat piece enters the approach in front of the machine, one shadowed light per room (the key). mat keys are Mats keys; 'marke' is the room's own violet glow, which breathes at idle, ramps with the forge and flares when the weapon comes out. Bilingual notices are in-world (1944 or the test range), never a real brand. T-254: `room` is the room round the machine in its own frame as the probe would find it (back: metres to the wall behind along +Z, ceil: the ceiling's height, left / right: metres to the side walls along the back wall; 99 = none): the fallback where no physics runs, replaced at load by rays (CrucibleRoom.probe_room). Any coordinate may be an anchor string instead of a number: ceil, back, left, right, top (the housing's top), w / -w (its half width), with an offset: \"ceil-0.04\", \"back-0.3\", \"-w-1.3\". `surround` is the housing that builds the machine into the room (style: brick, plate, concrete, hull, chrome, cradle; w / w_back: half widths beside the machine and behind z_back (default the plinth's back), narrowed at load to what stays off the navmesh; z0: its front face; top: the tallest it stands when the ceiling is higher; max_depth: further from the wall than this and the machine gets a stack on its own plinth instead; flue: collar, up, elbow, cap; arch, quoins, seams, straps, gauges, ash, wisp, stack: true / false; soot: 0..1).",
